add("HIS-10-04-17",ch10_04,"The Nuremberg Trials (1945-1946) were significant because:",["They established the precedent of holding individuals accountable for war crimes and crimes against humanity","They were held in Ethiopia","They were trials of Allied soldiers","They established the United Nations"],"a","The Nuremberg Trials prosecuted prominent Nazi leaders for war crimes, establishing important precedents in international law.","Medium")
add("HIS-10-04-18",ch10_04,"What was the Pan-African Congress of 1919?",["A meeting of European colonial powers","A conference in Paris organized by W.E.B. Du Bois to advocate for African rights","An Ethiopian diplomatic mission","A United Nations meeting"],"b","The Pan-African Congress of 1919, organized by W.E.B. Du Bois in Paris, demanded political rights, land rights, and self-determination for Africans.","Medium")
